            <ArticleTitle>Translation and cross-cultural adaptation of FFI to Brazilian Portuguese version: FFI - Brazil.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>398-405</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.rbr.2014.11.004</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0482-5004(15)00023-6</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Perform the translation and cultural adaptation of the questionnaire Foot Functional Index (FFI), which assesses the functionality of the foot, to the Brazilian Portuguese version.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">The Brazilian version development of FFI questionnaire was based on the guideline proposed by Guillemin. The applied process consisted of: (1) translation; (2) back-translation; (3) committee review; (4) pretesting. The Portuguese version was applied to 40 patients, both genders, aged over 18 years old, with plantar fasciitis and metatarsalgia to verify the level of the instrument comprehension. The final Brazilian version of the FFI was set after getting less than 15% of &quot;not understanding&quot; on each item.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Some terms and expressions were changed to obtain cultural equivalence for FFI. The terms that were incomprehensible were changed in accordance of patient suggestions.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">After the translation and cultural adaptation of the questionnaire, the final Portuguese version of FFI was concluded.</AbstractText>
